WEBVTT

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.760
I'm going on my break.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.570
I'm staying in Shizuoka until 
the third because of the snow.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:24.320
Hey, Rin-chan, I'm gonna be in 
Hamamatsu on the second and third.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.990
Want to come stay at my grandma's?

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:32.510
It's a really nice place by Lake Okuhamana.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Also, one of my friends 
there is supposed to come.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:47.770
Looking forward to it!!

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:43.600
Low Clearance

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.330
I'd like to stay the night.

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.020
That'll be 420 yen.

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.640
Please write your name and address here.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:58.720
<i>So cheap!</i>

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.500
<i>I've never seen a paid 
campground this inexpensive.</i>

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.860
<i>Thank goodness, though.</i>

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.900
<i>Now that I have a campsite...</i>

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:12.050
<i>Let's go check out the ocean!</i>

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:17.990
<b>Beach Access 
</b>(Omotehama Parkade)<b></b>

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.490
Hamana Bridge is huge...

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:36.510
<b>(2) Episode 3 
Surprise Camping and Some Deep Thoughts</b>

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.190
<i>There are quite a few people 
fishing over New Year's break.</i>

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:53.500
<i>This should be a good spot.</i>

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:34.320
<i>It's January, and yet the sand is so warm.</i>

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.830
<i></i>

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.620
<i>Reading all day on the beach, 
taking a hot spring bath...</i>

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.040
<i>Talk about living in luxury.</i>

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.020
<i>What's with the crowd?</i>

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.040
Pardon me.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.250
What is everyone doing here?

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.750
We're watching the sun 
set over the red torii.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:44.510
The sun sets right at the torii 
this time of the year. It's so pretty.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:56.930
<i>I saw the sunrise, then the sunset.</i>

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.320
<i>It's been such a chill New Year's.</i>

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.780
<i>We're meeting up at Sakume Station at eleven.</i>

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.370
<i>What should I take as a gift?</i>

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.660
<b>Kanzanji Temple Shizuka Strawberry Rice Cakes</b>

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.660
<b>Strawberry 
Shine</b>

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.270
<i>These strawberry rice cakes look good.</i>

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.330
Nadeshiko, it's time.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:29.300
We'll follow tomorrow in the car.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.590
Don't miss your transfers.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:32.560
Okay.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.490
You're not forgetting your gifts, are you?

00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:35.430
I got them.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.160
And your phone?

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.770
Don't worry.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.820
See you, Onee-chan.

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.530
Take care.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:46.110
Say hi to Rin-chan for me.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.910
Sure, will do!

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.120
Okay.

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:11.850
<b>Kanzanji Hot Springs</b>

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.850
<i>Here I am at Kanzanji.</i>

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.600
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.850
<b>Kigawa Eel</b>

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.350
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.100
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.100
<b>

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.100
Eel

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:22.110
<i>The eel pressure...</i>

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.110
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.110
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.110
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.110
Eel

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:27.110
<b>Eel</b>

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.250
<i>But if I give in, my wallet 
will suffer a violent death.</i>

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:29.360
Shizuka

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:29.140
<i>Found it.</i>

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.230
<i>I think I'm here a bit early.</i>

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:36.120
Please take a number if 
you arrive before opening.

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:35.660
<i>Number tickets?</i>

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.120
Please line up before opening.
Not valid if you are not in line.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.120
Number Ticket

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:47.490
<i>Oh, they were all waiting
 in their cars because it's cold.</i>

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.630
Good morning.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.410
We are now accepting orders 
for our Strawberry Shine.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.140
Please give your number when you order.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.590
I'll take fifty.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:57.920
I'd also like fifty.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.520
<i>What? Fifty?</i>

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:00.720
Fifty for me.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:04.010
<i>E-Everyone's buying that many?</i>

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:02.900
I'd like fifty, please!

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:04.520
Fifty, please!

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.130
Fifty here.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:07.780
<i>W-W-W-W-Wait...</i>

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.770
Fifty, please!

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:12.780
<i>Leave some for me! I just want four!</i>

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:14.800
Let's see...

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.290
One cream, please.

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:22.970
Actually, make that two!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:24.040
You got it.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:27.250
Shinjohara

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:26.800
Wait! Wait for me!

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.450
<i>And now I'm at Sakume Station.</i>

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.820
Hey! Rin-chan!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.620
Hey!

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:58.450
Sakume Station,
 Lake Hamana

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.760
Were you waiting long?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.450
No, I just got here.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.600
Happy New Year.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.760
I'm looking forward to 
another year of being friends.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.430
L-Likewise.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:08.210
I'm looking forward to it, too.

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:09.470
Oh, yeah.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:11.220
Over here, Rin-chan.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.900
Let me show you something.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:15.470
What is it?

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.040
Look at all of them.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.490
Aren't they cute? They're black-headed gulls.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:37.250
They always gather here 
in droves in the wintertime.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.540
Wow.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:41.090
They're so tame.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.820
<i>I like dogs, but birds are cute, too.</i>

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:49.220
Some of them have red feet,
and some of them have yellow feet.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.130
Oh, yeah.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:08.790
Nadeshiko, is your grandma's place nearby?

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.150
I think about twenty minutes on foot.

00:09:13.090 --> 00:09:15.580
Hey, wanna grab lunch first?

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.790
There's a really good eel place nearby.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:19.410
What?

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:22.840
<i>E-Eel!</i>

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:25.660
<i>1,290 yen remaining.</i>

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.660
1,290 yen remaining

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.940
Hello.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:33.170
W-Wait, Nadeshiko...

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.140
<i>Hang on...</i>

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:38.180
<i>Maybe this place is affordable.</i>

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:39.600
<i>Of course!</i>

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:43.460
<i>It's probably cheaper here 
because it's caught locally.</i>

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:43.930
Come on! This way!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.330
<i>That's it!</i>

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.670
<i>That must be it!</i>

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:48.440
<i>I get to have eel!</i>

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.820
<i>It already smells so yummy.</i>

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:03.200
Two top-grades, please.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:04.700
Two top-grades coming up.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.580
Yup. Top grade.

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.080
Top grade?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>1,800 yen</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>Regular</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>3,000 yen</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>High Quality</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>Top Grade</b>

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.840
<b>4,000 yen</b>

00:10:16.230 --> 00:10:18.250
N-N-Nadeshiko...

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.720
M-M-My money...

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.460
It's fine.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:26.220
I'll pick up the check.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:31.980
I told my dad you were coming to 
Grandma's with me, and he said...

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.400
She's been so good to you, Nadeshiko.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.610
Treat her to some good Lake Hamana eel.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.680
Then he gave me some money.

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:46.250
So you don't need to worry. 
You can just enjoy it.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:48.250
Th-Thank you.

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:11.020
<i>I never knew that's how you clean them.</i>

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.880
I can't stand the sight of blood.

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.030
Then why'd you pick a counter seat?

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:20.030
Your top-grade eel.

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:26.300
Well, shall we?

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:27.120
Yeah.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:29.540
Let's eat.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:37.320
<b>Ramune
200 yen</b>

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:37.320
<b>Non-alcoholic
Ayani Dry Zero
400 yen</b>

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.920
It's so good, huh, Rin-chan?

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.060
<i>Oh, no.</i>

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:49.770
<i>Now that I know what this tastes like,</i>

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:55.560
<i>I'm going to have to come 
back to Lake Hamana again.</i>

00:11:57.680 --> 00:11:59.570
<i>She's already done!</i>

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.570
<b>Eel</b>

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.570
Thank you.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.840
That was insanely good.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.040
Right?

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.330
That's Grandma's place over there.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.130
Grandma, I'm here!

00:12:25.130 --> 00:12:26.720
Thanks for having me.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.450
Ah, welcome, Nade-chan.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:32.230
Happy New Year.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.080
You, too.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.980
Thanks for coming all the way 
from Yamanashi, Rin-chan.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:38.860
Nice to meet you.

00:12:39.260 --> 00:12:40.610
It's a pleasure to be here.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.490
Been a while, Nadeshiko.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:47.560
Aya-chan! You're already here.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.760
This is Toki Ayano-chan.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.500
We've been friends since we were little.

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:57.960
Nice to meet you.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:06.230
I've seen lots of you in the camping 
photos Nadeshiko takes, Rin-chan.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:07.720
H-Hi.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.810
You should get under the kotatsu.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:11.150
It must have been cold.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:12.720
Yeah, I will!

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:16.480
<b>Lake Hamana Specialty 

00:13:13.130 --> 00:13:14.520
Oh, eel pie!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.480
And it's the kind with nuts!

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:21.000
Aya-chan brought them because 
she heard you were coming.

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:22.890
Thanks, Aya-chan.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.990
Don't eat all of them yourself.

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:28.830
Yum!

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:34.160
Nadeshiko really makes anything look good.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.250
<i>I know.</i>

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.440
Even if it's not anything that good,

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:41.380
when she eats it, it makes you 
want to ask for a bite yourself.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.000
<i>I totally get it.</i>

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:46.970
She used to make things 
look even better before.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.010
Before?

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:52.960
When is this photo from?

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:54.270
Our first year of middle school.

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:57.770
Nadeshiko's dad loves to eat.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:02.770
Maybe it's because they ate a lot together,
 but she was chubby until our third year.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:04.660
Until your third year?

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.880
How did you lose so much weight in a year?

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:11.700
I spent all summer lazing 
around and eating snacks,

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.540
and my sister finally snapped.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.540
That's enough eating, you pig!

00:14:16.810 --> 00:14:22.050
She made her do lap after lap 
on her bike around Lake Hamana.

00:14:22.050 --> 00:14:25.300
I thought my sister was a monster.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:28.320
But now you're fit and slim, thanks to her.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.420
I guess so...

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:36.560
I liked watching chubby 
Nadeshiko eating, though.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:39.310
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:41.780
<i>So that's the secret to how she had</i>

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:45.570
<i>the strength to bike from
Nanbucho to Lake Motosu.</i>

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:52.080
Although she still has doughy cheeks, 
even after losing weight.

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:53.830
Try it, Rin-chan.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:58.910
<i>I'm not even tugging that hard. So stretchy...</i>

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.520
Let me, too.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:12.840
Say, Nade-chan, you go 
camping a lot lately, right?

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:16.200
Tell us all about it.

00:15:16.200 --> 00:15:17.100
Okay!

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.770
This is from when we went Christmas camping.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.100
What a lovely place.

00:15:22.390 --> 00:15:26.110
This is the tomato sukiyaki 
that Aoi-chan made us.

00:15:26.470 --> 00:15:29.310
The Japanese breakfast I made.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.700
It's all just you guys cooking.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:34.660
Eating outdoors is the best part of camping.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.890
Right, Rin-chan?

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:38.240
Is it?

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.500
Want to try it out?

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:45.890
What's this?

00:15:45.890 --> 00:15:47.580
A mini offertory box.

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.130
It's a campfire grill.

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.840
Huh, so that's how it works.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:56.680
<b>Hot!</b>

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:56.680
Hot!

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:00.460
Is this yours, Aya-chan?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:01.520
Yeah.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.260
It's so cool!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.040
Try getting on.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.150
Can I?

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.560
Why are you grinning like you're all that?

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:17.660
Hey, they're done.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.040
Yummy!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.210
Okay, Nadeshiko.

00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:10.590
Let me know next time you're back.

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:13.840
I wish we could hang out a little longer.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:15.260
Don't blame me.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:18.090
The convenience store doesn't  
give me time off for New Year's.

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:24.230
Aya-chan! Wanna go to the 
observatory after work tonight?

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.640
The observatory?

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:32.010
Rin-chan.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:32.890
Rin-chan!

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.520
We should get going.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:39.760
Are you okay?

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.990
It's been three days since 
I last slept on proper bedding.

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:44.350
It's just so comfy...

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:57.060
It's pitch-black out here. Can you manage?

00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:57.940
Yeah.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.890
This place is like my back yard.

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.730
Hey.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:09.770
Aya-chan!

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.030
You guys are late.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:13.340
Sorry!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.780
How was work?

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.090
Bentenjima is around there.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:26.300
That bright spot is where 
Hamamatsu Station is.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.130
What's that?

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.990
The Lake Hamana service area.

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.770
I love the sight of Lake Hamana from here.

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:36.050
I used to bike up here all the time.

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.860
Remember, Aya-chan?

00:18:37.860 --> 00:18:40.700
I didn't come that often
 because it was exhausting.

00:18:42.630 --> 00:18:45.500
How was camping this time, Rin-chan?

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.060
A lot happened, but it was good.

00:18:51.480 --> 00:18:55.510
Going solo camping after 
Christmas made me realize

00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:00.160
that I still like camping by myself, too.

00:19:00.690 --> 00:19:04.400
It's camping all the same, but the 
outdoors is different when you're alone.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:08.210
The things you see, the things you eat...

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.300
And you get to spend time 
contemplating things.

00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:17.840
I think solo camping is a way 
to appreciate loneliness.

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.600
Loneliness, huh?

00:19:27.090 --> 00:19:29.160
Aya-chan, want some cocoa?

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:30.390
Oh, sure.

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:31.620
Look! I have ramen, too!

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:33.060
Look!

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:36.280
You're gonna gain weight again 
if you eat that before bedtime.

00:19:40.040 --> 00:19:40.700
Here.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.110
Thanks.

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:57.130
When I first heard you'd 
started camping in Yamanashi,

00:19:57.390 --> 00:20:05.220
honestly, I thought you were crazy 
for going camping out in the cold.

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:09.880
But after talking to you two today,
 I think I kind of get it.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.750
See you, Aya-chan.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.030
Yeah. Bye.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:29.940
Rin-chan, I'll come visit 
Yamanashi when it's warmer.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:33.860
I'll haul myself out there 
on my moped like you did.

00:20:42.240 --> 00:20:44.410
Okay, take care, Rin-chan.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:45.290
Yeah.

00:20:45.290 --> 00:20:46.800
See you after the break.

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:56.610
Thanks for coming to get me, Grandpa.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:57.560
Sure.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:59.940
Did you have fun this time?

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.120
Yeah.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.460
<b>Inuinu Inuko-san</b>

00:22:39.470 --> 00:22:41.460
Inuinu Inuko-san!

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:43.460
I've been thinking...

00:22:43.800 --> 00:22:47.930
Doesn't the name "Toyama" make it seem 
like that's where Mt. Fuji should be?

00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:49.470
Oh, yeah, it does.

00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:54.970
Toyama Prefecture

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:54.970
Apparently, some people think 
that's where Mt. Fuji actually is.

00:22:55.140 --> 00:22:59.690
Nadeshiko-chan, it's true that Mt. Fuji 
used to be in Toyama Prefecture.

00:22:59.690 --> 00:23:00.480
Huh?!

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:04.030
There was a tectonic shift 
thousands of years ago,

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:07.990
and it moved from Tateyama 
to where it is now.

00:23:08.120 --> 00:23:10.560
That's why Toyama's name...

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:12.010
Stare...

00:23:12.010 --> 00:23:13.110
You're lying.

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:14.990
I-I'm not lying!

00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.990
Just look at my eyes!

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:21.810
Stare...

00:23:22.950 --> 00:23:24.760
Yeah, you're totally lying.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>What Are You Buying With Your Temp Job Money?</b>

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:35.260
<b>What Are You Buying With Your Temp Job Money?</b>

